.00945281982421875, -0.0025157928466796875, 0.0226593017578125, 0.00757598876953125, -0.006298065185546875, 0.028289794921875, -0.036865234375, 0.015289306640625, 0.00862884521484375, -0.0030345916748046875, 0.0213470458984375, -0.002391815185546875, 0.03997802734375, -0.0023937225341796875, 0.051055908203125, 0.00467681884765625, 0.041473388671875, -0.00646209716796875, -0.0009670257568359375, 0.00189208984375, -0.0157318115234375, 0.007114410400390625, -0.00047659873962402344, -0.020477294921875, 0.0220184326171875, 0.04998779296875, -0.019500732421875, -0.0164031982421875, -0.031585693359375, 0.02215576171875, -0.02227783203125, 0.00365447998046875, 0.047515869140625, 0.035308837890625, 0.0016279220581054688, -0.034088134765625, -0.0103302001953125, -0.0089263916015625, 0.00870513916015625, -0.0264129638671875, 0.01499176025390625, -0.0167388916015625, -0.0225982666015625, -0.0124969482421875, -0.00982666015625, 0.033538818359375, 0.01213836669921875, -0.01158905029296875, -0.007259368896484375], "payload": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "text": "Large-scale image generation has progressed through advances in data scale, quality, rebalancing, and recaptioning. However, conventional pipelines typically optimize task-specific datasets independently. The main challenge is not only curating each task-specific corpus, but also organizing heterogeneous supervision based on the dependencies among generative capabilities. We propose a \\textbf{capability-driven data infrastructure} that unifies capability-specific supervision construction with capability-aligned curriculum scheduling. This infrastructure consists of three specialized yet interoperable data engines that provide complementary relational supervision for text-image grounding, inter-image transformation, and image-knowledge association. Caption experts further align text-to-image (T2I) and editing supervision across tasks and levels of granularity. A multi-stage curriculum jointly evolves task composition, visual concept distribution, data quality, and image resolution according to the dependency order of capability acquisition. Capability-aware evaluation completes the loop through targeted retrieval, expert construction, and gap-aware resampling. At scale, this framework curates a 440M-image T2I corpus, 120M editing pairs, and over 27M image-entity pairs. Using this infrastructure, we train multimodal diffusion models from scratch at two scales, with 3B and 6B parameters, respectively. We conduct quantitative evaluation on CPI-Bench, as well as qualitative assessments across diverse text-to-image and editing scenarios. Experimental results demonstrate broad visual coverage, versatile rendering, and effective transfer across generative capabilities."}}